  "limits": "One unpaced local release-mode run, single host thread, uncontrolled OS/desktop scheduling. Per row: load N entries from pre-built Values (timed; heap growth counted by a counting allocator), then 1,000 single queries spread over the table (JSON text parsing excluded, output Value construction included). Queries: places nearby (max_distance 8; every field is in one valley, so each answer counts all N siblings), timeline query known_to, things move, species pet, recipes check, communities check_relation, actions describe, lore select, inventory rows, info lookup, evidence select, facts check. Things, species, recipes, communities and actions run their stateless workflow, which returns the whole table on every call, so their per-call cost grows with the table. Facts are loaded by registering one at a time. Excludes the gamectx local CLI, cross-module wiring, model calls and engine work; not a whole-game or realtime guarantee."
